Objective: 
Find the password in the data.txt file which contains base64 encoded data.

Commands used:
ls - Lists contents of the current directory.
man base64 - Manual for the command base64.
base64 --help - Helps with the use by giving you usage, arguments and options.
base64 -d data.txt - decodes the base64 encoded text.

Thought process:
This doesn't seem too hard so i used ls and the file was there.
I used man base64 and read through till i came across -d which is --decode and its supposed to decode encoded text.
So i wasn't 100% sure how to use it so i did base64 --help and i understood how it worked.
Then did base64 -d data.txt and there it was.

